{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/920124-rules-idea-doing-away-with-attributes","id":920124,"title":"Rules Idea: Doing Away With Attributes?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-23T20:52:55-07:00","id":920124,"title":"Rules Idea: Doing Away With Attributes?","content":"Has anyone ever spared any thought towards giving characters ratings in Physical/Mental/Social and Power/Finesse/Resistance, rather than the nine distinct Attributes? I've got no mind for the math involved, but I'm curious enough about the idea to float it out here. I'm kind of fond of the idea, as it spares us from the current of Primary Social characters inevitably having an average/low rating in one of those three Attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T20:57:22-07:00","id":920126,"title":"","content":"You have my curiosity. Go on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11854-dibastet","name":"DiBastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T22:48:55-07:00","id":920185,"title":"","content":"Some problems you run into (rather quickly, if I way add):<br /> \u2022 Naively swapping it so you just replace Attributes with the sum of the two appropriate Attributes (replacing Strength with Physical + Power, for example) results in <i>incredibly</i> high equivalent Attributes really quickly.<br /> \u2022 How much are they going to cost? Each dot of a new Attribute is worth <i>three</i> dots of old Attributes.<br /> \u2022 What's the cap? The system doesn't <i>like</i> large dice-pools, so just letting them cap at 5 <i>might</i> result in problems.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Another naive implementation would be using the higher of the two - but then you just pump one set of Attributes. If you use the lower of the two, then everything costs twice as much.<br /> \u2022 Maybe we use the higher for dicepools, and the lower for derived values? So Defense would be the lowest of Physical, Mental, and Finesse, you'd have Health Levels equal to the lower of your Physical and Resistance, but attacking with a knife would be (higher of Physical and Power) + Melee.<br /> \u2022 That sounds kinda workable - you'd have to fiddle with the costs a bit (maybe reduce it 3xp per dot?)<br /> <br /> Other ideas:<br /> \u2022 It would greatly simplify all the rules for Ephemeral Beings - now everyone shares at least three of their traits!<br /> \u2022 Claimed would just replace the host's &quot;approach&quot; attributes with their own. Which would give you a big ol' boost to dice pools, and <i>maybe</i> a little boost to derived stuff like HLs.<br /> \u2022 If you got your hands on Numina or Influences somehow, just use Power/Finesse/Resistance.<br /> <br /> So, basically, it ends up being weird - I'd say everyone starts at two dots in each Attributes, with three dots to split between them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T04:46:46-07:00","id":920286,"title":"","content":"I thought that having to have at least one average/low Attribute even in your primary set was the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T06:51:19-07:00","id":920336,"title":"","content":"So, prototyping this on the fly, because it's an interesting idea but I've never seen it done before: <br /> <br /> You have three Techniques: Power, Finesse, and Resistance. Each starts at 1, and cannot go above 3. Each costs 15xp to raise.<br /> You have three Areas: Mental, Physical, and Social. Each starts at 0, and cannot go above 2. Each costs 15xp to raise.<br /> At character creation, you get 4 points to split between Techniques and Areas. <br /> <br /> Example starting builds:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Susan Strongarm puts 2 in Power, 2 in Physical. Translated stats:<br /> Int: 3<br /> Wit: 1<br /> Res: 1<br /> Str: 5<br /> Dex: 3<br /> Sta: 3<br /> Pre: 3<br /> Man: 1<br /> Com: 1<br /> <br /> Joe Cool puts 2 in Social, 2 in Mental. Translated stats:<br /> Int: 3<br /> Wit: 3<br /> Res: 3<br /> Str: 1<br /> Dex: 1<br /> Sta: 1<br /> Pre: 3<br /> Man: 3<br /> Com: 3<br /> <br /> Alex Clever puts 2 in Finesse, 1 in Physical, 1 in Social. Translated stats:<br /> Int: 1<br /> Wit: 3<br /> Res: 1<br /> Str: 2<br /> Dex: 4<br /> Sta: 2<br /> Pre: 2<br /> Man: 4<br /> Com: 2<br /> <br /> Cid Av puts 1 in Power, 1 in Finesse, 2 in Resistance. Translated stats: <br /> Int: 2<br /> Wit: 2<br /> Res: 3<br /> Str: 2<br /> Dex: 2<br /> Sta: 3<br /> Pre: 2<br /> Man: 2<br /> Com: 3<br /> <br /> Ida No puts 1 in Finesse, 1 in Resistance, 1 in Physical, 1 in Social. Translated stats:<br /> Int: 1<br /> Wit: 2<br /> Res: 2<br /> Str: 2<br /> Dex: 3<br /> Sta: 3<br /> Pre: 2<br /> Man: 3<br /> Com: 3<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> XP-wise, this works out the same as standard CC (putting 3, 4, and 5 in Attributes is a total of 12; each Technique/Area affects 3 Attributes, so 4 Tech/Area points = 12 Attribute points).<br /> <br /> However, it's no longer possible to get the same sort of spread as standard creation; you're basically forced into average across the board, or very specialized. I dunno if I like this or not. (At 15xp per point, it does make it a lot slower to advance, but any cheaper and it doesn't mechanically balance with system-as-written.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T07:19:11-07:00","id":920352,"title":"","content":"Huh. I was bouncing around a similar idea. Basically, you have a Power/Finesse/Resistance or Physical/Mental/Social spread, then tack on +/- Physical/Mental/Social or +/- Power/Finesse/Resistance, respectively to tweak areas that might be stronger or weaker than the average. No idea on how to XP price it though. My original concept was for solely building organizations, and the +/- thing was a tradeoff (so, say it had Power 3, Finesse 2, Resistance 2. You could take a -1 Mental and a -1 Social (or a -2 Social) to get a +2 Physical. That would lead to Str: 5, Dex: 4, Sta: 4, Int: 2, Wit: 1, Res: 1, Pre: 2, Man: 1, Com: 1).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T08:26:24-07:00","id":920379,"title":"","content":"How about just picking one axis, such as going with physical/mental/social to contrast with ephemeral entities using power/finesse/resistance, and if you want some extra granularity use Attribute Specialties. So, for example, you might have 3 dots in Physical with a Specialty in Dexterity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-24-2016, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T08:58:02-07:00","id":920389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/920124-rules-idea-doing-away-with-attributes?p=920379#post920379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about just picking one axis, such as going with physical/mental/social to contrast with ephemeral entities using power/finesse/resistance</div> </div> </div> </div>I would take it in the other direction, since I enjoy the idea that everyone has the same stats. I say power/finesse/resistance with attribute specialties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11854-dibastet","name":"DiBastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T09:04:14-07:00","id":920391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DiBastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/920124-rules-idea-doing-away-with-attributes?p=920389#post920389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would take it in the other direction, since I enjoy the idea that everyone has the same stats. I say power/finesse/resistance with attribute specialties.</div> </div> </div> </div>That works too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}